From 1f313504377b253bbd395173c610a8816043bd11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vishwajitvm <vishwajitmall50@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:42:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(templates): an empty CORS_ORIGINS fails as a normal
 env issue, not a crash

With CORS_ORIGINS= (empty), a generated app refused to boot with
"Unexpected error: defineEnv(schema): asynchronous validators are not
supported for env" (exit 1) instead of naming the key. Zod 4 still runs
the object's superRefine when a field failed its own check, so the
refinement got the raw string '' and called .some() on it; the throw
made Zod's Standard Schema validate() fall back to its async path, which
defineEnv rightly refuses.

The generated refinement now checks only a real list. Found by a boot
matrix (every .env.example key missing / empty / malformed) on a fresh
app with every package installed. Regression test runs the generated
schema with the real Zod, through the same Standard Schema validate()
that defineEnv uses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: vishwajitvm <vishwajitmall50@gmail.com>
